# Game Specification

## Vision

A 30–45 minute graphical Infocom-style mystery.

## Player Interaction

Commands use VERB NOUN or VERB NOUN WITH NOUN.
Required verbs: look, examine, take, drop, use, open, talk, inventory.

## World

Six interconnected rooms.
The player begins in the study.
Room connections must always be internally consistent.

## State

Track player location, inventory, object locations, unlocked passages,
NPC dialogue progress, solved puzzles, and ending state.

## Inventory

No inventory capacity limit.

## Puzzles

Two puzzles.
Every required item must remain obtainable.
The game must not enter an unwinnable state.

## Interface

Use pygame-ce and pygame-gui.
Scrollable transcript, command entry, inventory panel, location name,
and an internal map visualization.

## Architecture

Parser and world rules must not import pygame or pygame_gui.
Only the application and presentation layers may use GUI objects.

## Completion

A winning command sequence must be documented and executable.

## Non-goals

No combat, real-time deadline, procedural generation, or external assets.
